  "notes": "Independent quality-reviewer sub-agent review. Verified: (1) HTTP client -> in-process swaps correct (ProctorSessionService.open -> SessionService.checkProctorAssignment; ProctorCommandService.issueCommand -> AttemptService.forceSubmit), and the now-redundant NotAssignedToSessionException/ProctorAssignmentCheckFailedException were correctly dropped (no references remain). (2) No outbox/ProcessedEvent/AMQP event-backbone anywhere in either module; ViolationService/EnrollmentService publish plain ApplicationEventPublisher events inside their own @Transactional methods, notification's 3 listeners are @TransactionalEventListener (AFTER_COMMIT default) matching the 'publish only after commit succeeds' constraint. (3) UserDirectoryEntry/repository/consumer (forbidden artifacts) fully absent; NotificationDispatchService resolves recipients via IdentityService only, User entity exposure across the identity boundary is a pre-existing IdentityService.findById pattern being reused, not a new precedent. (4) Missing-recipient policy is an explicit logged skip, no directory-row resurrection anywhere. (5) Every host/proctor-facing read stays tenant-scoped. (6) Cross-module event types (ViolationDetectedEvent in proctoring, StudentEnrolledEvent in session, AttemptPublishedEvent in notification) all carry correct @NamedInterface package-info; ModuleStructureTest passes 3/3. (7) Exactly one global SecurityConfig/JwtDecoder bean (identity module); proctoring defines no duplicate security chain; STOMP role check remains the single enforcement point since @PreAuthorize doesn't apply to @MessageMapping. (8) AttemptPublishedNotificationListener is clearly documented as an intentional forward-looking deferral (no publisher until Phase 10 reporting exists), consistent with prior-phase precedent. Full suite 428/428 green, ModuleStructureTest 3/3 passes.",
